knight's second square.} 11. Ke7 {The king, at the adverse king's second square.} Kg8 {The king,
at his knight's square.} 12. Kf6 {The king, at the adverse king's bishop's third square.} Kh7
{The king, at his rook's second square.} 13. Kf7 {The king, at the adverse king's bishop's
second square.} Kh8 {The king, at his rook's square.} 14. Kxg6 {The king takes the pawn.} Kg8
{The king, at his knight's square.} 15. Kf6 {The king, at the adverse king's bishop's third
